From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: define HEVC 4:4:4 DXVA GUIDs for v13 mingw snapshots

VLC only defines DXVA_ModeHEVC_VLD_Main_444 / Main10_444 / Main12_444 when
__MINGW64_VERSION_MAJOR < 13, assuming every v13 toolchain ships them in
<dxva.h>. The HEVC 4:4:4 Range Extension GUIDs were actually added to
mingw-w64's dxva.h after the v13 ABI bump, so v13 snapshots taken before that
commit (e.g. the mingw-w64 bundled in llvm-mingw 20240619, which we pin for the
up-to-date d3d11/DXGI headers) report major version 13 yet still lack these
three GUIDs. That leaves directx_va.c referencing undeclared identifiers.

Split the fallback so the 4:4:4 GUIDs are provided for anything below v14 while
the 4:2:2 GUIDs keep their original < 13 guard. On a toolchain whose header
already defines the 4:4:4 GUIDs this block is skipped, so no redefinition can
occur for our pinned toolchain.
---
 modules/codec/avcodec/directx_va.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/codec/avcodec/directx_va.c b/modules/codec/avcodec/directx_va.c
--- a/modules/codec/avcodec/directx_va.c
+++ b/modules/codec/avcodec/directx_va.c
@@ -80,6 +80,10 @@
 DEFINE_GUID(DXVA_ModeHEVC_VLD_Main12,        0x1a72925f, 0x0c2c, 0x4f15, 0x96, 0xfb, 0xb1, 0x7d, 0x14, 0x73, 0x60, 0x3f);
 DEFINE_GUID(DXVA_ModeHEVC_VLD_Main10_422,    0x0bac4fe5, 0x1532, 0x4429, 0xa8, 0x54, 0xf8, 0x4d, 0xe0, 0x49, 0x53, 0xdb);
 DEFINE_GUID(DXVA_ModeHEVC_VLD_Main12_422,    0x55bcac81, 0xf311, 0x4093, 0xa7, 0xd0, 0x1c, 0xbc, 0x0b, 0x84, 0x9b, 0xee);
+#endif
+// HEVC 4:4:4 Range Extension GUIDs landed in mingw-w64 dxva.h after the v13 ABI
+// bump; some v13 toolchain snapshots (e.g. llvm-mingw 20240619) still lack them.
+#if __MINGW64_VERSION_MAJOR < 14
 DEFINE_GUID(DXVA_ModeHEVC_VLD_Main_444,      0x4008018f, 0xf537, 0x4b36, 0x98, 0xcf, 0x61, 0xaf, 0x8a, 0x2c, 0x1a, 0x33);
 DEFINE_GUID(DXVA_ModeHEVC_VLD_Main10_444,    0x0dabeffa, 0x4458, 0x4602, 0xbc, 0x03, 0x07, 0x95, 0x65, 0x9d, 0x61, 0x7c);
 DEFINE_GUID(DXVA_ModeHEVC_VLD_Main12_444,    0x9798634d, 0xfe9d, 0x48e5, 0xb4, 0xda, 0xdb, 0xec, 0x45, 0xb3, 0xdf, 0x01);
